+ Linux Processes & Services 
  - Commands line
    ps: Show your terminal processes
    ps aux or tesk manager in kali : Show all system processes
    top: Live process & system monitor
    htop: Better version of top. top and htop type of wireshark
    systemctl list-units --type=service: Show active system services
---------------------------------------------------------------
    Learn:
    Process = running program
    Service = background program (like SSH, Apache)
    Why services matter (they open ports = attack surface)
    Example:
    If Apache is running → port 80 open → web attack possible.
+ Understand Vulnerabilities (30 minutes)
    Learn these basic ideas:
    Vulnerability = weakness
    Exploit = method to use the weakness
    Common beginner vulnerabilities:
    - Weak passwords
    - Open ports
    - Outdated software
    - Misconfigured permissions
    Real example:
    FTP allows anonymous login → attacker logs in without password.

